WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.072
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online B two, Book two.

2
00:00:05.372 --> 00:00:08.897
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.197 --> 00:00:16.087
Unit twenty-three: The Gig Economy. Today you will contrast ideas with 'although' and 'however'.

4
00:00:16.387 --> 00:00:19.040
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:23.291
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.150 --> 00:00:25.221
Gig economy.

7
00:00:26.217 --> 00:00:29.772
Gig economy means work made of short jobs, often through apps.

8
00:00:30.383 --> 00:00:32.511
The gig economy is growing fast.

9
00:00:33.117 --> 00:00:36.024
Your turn. Say: Gig economy.

10
00:00:38.867 --> 00:00:40.170
Gig economy.

11
00:00:40.917 --> 00:00:41.987
Freelance.

12
00:00:42.983 --> 00:00:46.527
Freelance means working for different clients, not one boss.

13
00:00:47.117 --> 00:00:48.954
She is a freelance designer.

14
00:00:49.550 --> 00:00:52.017
Your turn. Say: Freelance.

15
00:00:54.867 --> 00:00:55.833
Freelance.

16
00:00:56.583 --> 00:00:57.097
App.

17
00:00:58.083 --> 00:01:00.036
App means a program on a phone.

18
00:01:00.650 --> 00:01:02.859
Drivers find customers through an app.

19
00:01:03.450 --> 00:01:05.708
Your turn. Say: App.

20
00:01:08.567 --> 00:01:09.278
App.

21
00:01:10.017 --> 00:01:10.960
Flexible.

22
00:01:11.950 --> 00:01:14.286
Flexible means able to change easily.

23
00:01:14.883 --> 00:01:16.825
Gig work has flexible hours.

24
00:01:17.417 --> 00:01:20.359
Your turn. Say: Flexible.

25
00:01:23.200 --> 00:01:24.155
Flexible.

26
00:01:24.917 --> 00:01:25.767
Income.

27
00:01:26.783 --> 00:01:28.493
Income means money you earn.

28
00:01:29.083 --> 00:01:31.071
His income changes every month.

29
00:01:31.683 --> 00:01:34.452
Your turn. Say: Income.

30
00:01:37.300 --> 00:01:38.220
Income.

31
00:01:38.983 --> 00:01:39.857
Contract.

32
00:01:40.850 --> 00:01:42.908
Contract means a written work agreement.

33
00:01:43.517 --> 00:01:45.632
Read the contract before you sign.

34
00:01:46.217 --> 00:01:49.252
Your turn. Say: Contract.

35
00:01:52.100 --> 00:01:53.008
Contract.

36
00:01:53.750 --> 00:01:54.786
Benefits.

37
00:01:55.783 --> 00:01:59.373
Benefits means extras from work, like health insurance.

38
00:01:59.983 --> 00:02:02.180
Many gig workers have no benefits.

39
00:02:02.783 --> 00:02:05.227
Your turn. Say: Benefits.

40
00:02:08.067 --> 00:02:09.323
Benefits.

41
00:02:10.083 --> 00:02:11.131
Security.

42
00:02:12.117 --> 00:02:14.732
Security means being safe and stable.

43
00:02:15.317 --> 00:02:17.502
Job security matters to families.

44
00:02:18.117 --> 00:02:20.769
Your turn. Say: Security.

45
00:02:23.633 --> 00:02:24.681
Security.

46
00:02:25.467 --> 00:02:29.059
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:29.917 --> 00:02:32.392
Visal, what do you think of the gig economy?

48
00:02:33.483 --> 00:02:37.840
Gig work is flexible; however, income is not stable.

49
00:02:38.950 --> 00:02:40.032
Would you do it?

50
00:02:41.117 --> 00:02:44.277
Although I like freedom, I want job security.

51
00:02:45.383 --> 00:02:46.918
What about benefits?

52
00:02:48.017 --> 00:02:55.020
Freelancers earn well sometimes; however, they often have no benefits.

53
00:02:56.167 --> 00:02:57.911
Part three: grammar.

54
00:02:58.750 --> 00:03:01.191
Grammar focus: Although and however.

55
00:03:01.491 --> 00:03:02.654
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:03.350 --> 00:03:06.534
Gig work is flexible; however, income is not stable.

57
00:03:07.450 --> 00:03:10.355
Although I like freedom, I want security.

58
00:03:11.250 --> 00:03:14.643
Although apps make it easy, workers have few benefits.

59
00:03:15.600 --> 00:03:22.745
Use 'although' inside one sentence. Use 'however' to start a new idea, after a full stop or a semicolon, with a comma after it.

60
00:03:23.483 --> 00:03:28.736
Be careful! Don't say: Although gig work is flexible, but income is not stable.

61
00:03:30.700 --> 00:03:34.720
Say: Although gig work is flexible, income is not stable.

62
00:03:35.020 --> 00:03:36.532
Don't use 'but' with 'although'.

63
00:03:37.333 --> 00:03:39.962
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:40.767 --> 00:03:41.849
Work on Demand.

65
00:03:42.149 --> 00:03:45.263
In the gig economy, people find short jobs through an app.

66
00:03:46.267 --> 00:03:50.147
Freelance work is flexible; however, income can change every month.

67
00:03:51.133 --> 00:03:55.408
Although gig workers choose their hours, they often have no contract.

68
00:03:56.400 --> 00:03:58.806
Many of them have no benefits or security.

69
00:03:59.800 --> 00:04:03.216
Young workers should think about both sides before they choose.

70
00:04:04.300 --> 00:04:08.255
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:09.117 --> 00:04:12.358
Gig work is flexible; blank, income is not stable.

72
00:04:12.658 --> 00:04:16.312
A, however. B, although. C, because.

73
00:04:19.867 --> 00:04:21.669
The answer is A: however.

74
00:04:22.817 --> 00:04:24.375
Money you earn is blank.

75
00:04:24.675 --> 00:04:28.247
A, income. B, security. C, contract.

76
00:04:31.800 --> 00:04:33.602
The answer is A: income.

77
00:04:34.750 --> 00:04:38.085
Working for different clients, not one boss, is blank work.

78
00:04:38.385 --> 00:04:42.619
A, freelance. B, secure. C, contract.

79
00:04:46.167 --> 00:04:48.398
The answer is A: freelance.

80
00:04:49.600 --> 00:04:52.519
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

81
00:04:53.383 --> 00:04:55.429
What are the pros and cons of gig work?

82
00:05:04.217 --> 00:05:05.694
Now listen to Visal.

83
00:05:05.994 --> 00:05:16.634
Gig work is flexible, so you can choose your hours. However, the income is not stable, and although some jobs pay well, there are usually no benefits.

84
00:05:16.934 --> 00:05:18.631
Excellent answer, Visal!

85
00:05:19.517 --> 00:05:23.655
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and although and however.

86
00:05:23.955 --> 00:05:29.614
Today's value is economic awareness. Understand how money and work affect your life choices.

87
00:05:29.914 --> 00:05:32.903
See you in Unit twenty-four. Goodbye!

88
00:05:33.203 --> 00:05:36.030
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

